  "abstract": "ICEWS Coded Event Data — Conflict Quadrant (1995-2022). General-purpose, machine-coded political event data (CAMEO ontology) derived from global news coverage, 1995-2022 (discontinued 11 April 2023). Restricted to CAMEO's \"Conflict\" quadrant — verbal conflict (demand, disapprove, reject, threaten, protest, exhibit force posture, reduce relations) and material conflict (coerce, assault, fight, unconventional mass violence). This is NOT a slavery/war-curated dataset — it is included as broad supporting/contextual coverage so conflict and slavery records can be cross-referenced against the wider political-conflict landscape at the same place and time. Harmonised copy produced by cdisaw-parquet: the (CD)ISaW ingest script for this source was run unchanged against a Parquet writer instead of PostGIS, giving 5,796,392 event rows in the wide 35-column layout (wide/) and an 18-column crws-nodes projection (crws/). Dataset-level domain: context.",
